{
  "an3.70:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.70 ",
  "an3.70:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "an3.70:0.3": "Sabbath ",
  "an3.70:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an3.70:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in the stilt longhouse of Migāra’s mother in the Eastern Monastery. ",
  "an3.70:1.3": "Then Visākhā, Migāra’s mother, went up to the Buddha, bowed, and sat down to one side. The Buddha said to her, ",
  "an3.70:1.4": "“So, Visākhā, where are you coming from in the middle of the day?” ",
  "an3.70:1.5": "“Today, sir, I’m observing the sabbath.” ",
  "an3.70:2.1": "“There are, Visākhā, these three sabbaths. ",
  "an3.70:2.2": "What three? ",
  "an3.70:2.3": "The sabbath of the cowherds, the sabbath of the Jains, and the sabbath of the noble ones. ",
  "an3.70:2.4": "And what is the sabbath of the cowherds? ",
  "an3.70:2.5": "It’s just like a cowherd who, in the late afternoon, takes the cows back to their owners. They reflect: ",
  "an3.70:2.6": "‘Today the cows grazed in this spot and that, and they drank in this spot and that. ",
  "an3.70:2.7": "Tomorrow the cows will graze in this spot and that, and drink in this spot and that.’ ",
  "an3.70:2.8": "In the same way, someone keeping the sabbath reflects: ",
  "an3.70:2.9": "‘Today I ate this and that, and had a meal of this and that. ",
  "an3.70:2.10": "Tomorrow I’ll eat this and that, and have a meal of this and that.’ ",
  "an3.70:2.11": "And so they spend their day with a mind full of covetousness. ",
 